  "note": "Election of the Warrenpoint Urban District Council, 18 September 1946. There were 18 candidates for the 15 seats. East Ward (5 seats) and West Ward (7 seats) were both polled; only the elected candidates were printed, so the defeated candidates are not recorded. Labour had a majority of two on the new council; Edward Caulfield (N.), the retiring chairman, was among the defeated candidates whose totals were not printed."
